GET /index.php?module=jjwg_Maps&entryPoint=jjwg_Maps&cron=1&display_module=Accounts HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:33116
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 cvehunter-stage10

# No Cookie header -- entryPoint 'jjwg_Maps' is registered `auth => false`
# (modules/jjwg_Maps/entry_point_registry.php:2), so SugarApplication::execute()
# skips loadUser()/ACLFilter()/checkHTTPReferer() entirely. This single
# anonymous GET reaches jjwg_Maps_Router.php:14-25, which -- because
# $_REQUEST['cron'] is non-empty -- instantiates jjwg_MapsController and calls
# action_geocode_addresses() (controller.php:171-313), an unauthenticated
# batch job with no $current_user / ACL check anywhere in it.
